From 78e85ec001b05c28b54a03bdd50b91ce26f9c0a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:32:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtk-soc: allowed modes and the initial attach APN through
 MIPC

The modem does not register on LTE without an initial attach (initial EPS
bearer) APN, which the stock RIL sets with MIPC APN_SET_IA_REQ at boot;
ModemManager had no way to set it and no allowed-mode support.

Implement set_initial_eps_bearer_settings with APN_SET_IA_REQ and
set_current_modes with NW_SET_RAT_REQ, both in the stock RIL's wire format
(traced 2026-10-20) and sent on their own MIPC control channel
(/dev/ttyCMIPC2) so they do not interfere with the data bearer's channel.
Current values are read back with AT+ERAT? and AT+CGDCONT? (context 0).
Only the observed values are supported: LTE only or the modem default
(NR/LTE/3G/2G); IPv4v6 without credentials for the attach APN.
